{{define "article"}}<article class="doc" data-page="mcp">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/docs/">Docs</a></li><li>Connect</li><li aria-current="page">MCP (any harness)</li></ol>
    <h1>MCP (any harness)</h1>
    <p class="doc-lede">Any MCP client that speaks streamable HTTP can use the tools. One URL, no account, and no key to {{if .Auth}}try{{else}}use{{end}} the public tools.</p>
  </header>
  <details class="toc" data-toc open>
    <summary><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chev"/></svg>On this page</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#mcp-connect">Connect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mcp-skill">Agent skill</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mcp-tools">What the server lists</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mcp-result">Reading a result</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mcp-local">Run it locally (stdio)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mcp-limits">Limits</a></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="toc-more"><a href="https://discord.gg/XZzkH38dt9"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-discord"/></svg>Ask on Discord</a><a href="#top"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-up"/></svg>Back to top</a></div>
  </details>
  <div class="doc-body prose">
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Endpoint</dt><dd><code>{{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp</code></dd>
      <dt>Transport</dt><dd>Streamable HTTP, stateless, JSON responses. One JSON-RPC 2.0 message per POST; <code>GET</code> and <code>DELETE</code> answer 405.</dd>
      <dt>Auth</dt><dd>None {{if .Auth}}to try the public tools (trial limits){{else}}for public tools{{end}}. Optional: <code>X-Janice-Key</code> for a Janice appraisal with <code>appraise_items</code>. {{if .Auth}}{{if .SelfServe}}A free{{else}}An{{end}} API key for {{if .Auth}}daily use and the keyed {{plural .Stats.Keyed "tool" "tools"}}{{else}}keyed tools{{end}}, sent as <code>Authorization: Bearer ecd_...</code> or <code>X-API-Key: ecd_...</code>. With Claude Code: add <code>--header "X-API-Key: ecd_…"</code> to the <code>claude mcp add</code> command.{{else}}An API key for keyed tools (none issued yet).{{end}}</dd>
      <dt>Rate limit</dt><dd><b>{{.Lim.MCP}} requests per minute</b>{{if .KeysRaise}}{{if .AnonCap}} and {{.AnonCap}} a day{{end}} per client without a key; {{.KeyMCP}} per minute{{if .KeyCap}} and {{.KeyCap}} a day{{end}} with one{{else}} per caller{{end}}</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2 id="mcp-connect">Connect<a class="h-anchor" href="#mcp-connect" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
    <div class="code" data-tabs data-tab-group="mcp" data-copy-scope>
      <div class="code-head">
        <div class="code-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Client">
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="cli">Claude Code</button>
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="desktop">Claude.ai</button>
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="cursor">Cursor</button>
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="vscode">VS Code</button>
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="codex">Codex</button>
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="gemini">Gemini</button>
          <button class="code-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="json">JSON</button>
        </div>
        <button class="code-copy" type="button" data-copy aria-label="Copy"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><span data-copy-label>Copy</span></button>
      </div>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="cli"><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy>$ </span>claude mcp add --transport http --scope user eve-cyno {{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp</code></pre>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="desktop" hidden><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy># Customize &gt; Connectors &gt; Add custom connector. Paste this {{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp and choose “No sign-in”.</span>
{{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp
{{if .Auth}}<span class="tk-p" data-nocopy># If the dialog shows “Request headers” and you have a key: add the header x-api-key, with the key as its value.</span>
{{end}}<span class="tk-p" data-nocopy># Team and Enterprise: an owner adds it under Organization settings &gt; Connectors.</span></code></pre>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="cursor" hidden><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy># ~/.cursor/mcp.json</span>
{
  <span class="tk-k">"mcpServers"</span>: {
    <span class="tk-k">"eve-cyno"</span>: {
      <span class="tk-k">"url"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"{{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp"</span>{{if .Auth}},
      <span class="tk-k">"headers"</span>: {
        <span class="tk-k">"X-API-Key"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"&lt;your EVE-Cyno API key, optional&gt;"</span>
      }{{end}}
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="vscode" hidden><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy>// .vscode/mcp.json</span>
{{"{"}}{{if .Auth}}
  <span class="tk-k">"inputs"</span>: [
    {
      <span class="tk-k">"type"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"promptString"</span>,
      <span class="tk-k">"id"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"eve-cyno-key"</span>,
      <span class="tk-k">"description"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"EVE-Cyno API key (optional)"</span>,
      <span class="tk-k">"password"</span>: true
    }
  ],{{end}}
  <span class="tk-k">"servers"</span>: {
    <span class="tk-k">"eve-cyno"</span>: {
      <span class="tk-k">"type"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"http"</span>,
      <span class="tk-k">"url"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"{{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp"</span>{{if .Auth}},
      <span class="tk-k">"headers"</span>: {
        <span class="tk-k">"X-API-Key"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"${input:eve-cyno-key}"</span>
      }{{end}}
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="codex" hidden><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy>$ </span>codex mcp add eve-cyno --url {{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp</code></pre>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="gemini" hidden><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy>$ </span>gemini mcp add -s user -t http eve-cyno {{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp</code></pre>
<pre role="tabpanel" data-panel="json" hidden><code>{
  <span class="tk-k">"mcpServers"</span>: {
    <span class="tk-k">"eve-cyno"</span>: {
      <span class="tk-k">"type"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"http"</span>,
      <span class="tk-k">"url"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"{{.Origin}}{{.Prefix}}/mcp"</span>,
      <span class="tk-k">"headers"</span>: {
        <span class="tk-k">"X-Janice-Key"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"&lt;your Janice key, optional&gt;"</span>{{if .Auth}},
        <span class="tk-k">"X-API-Key"</span>: <span class="tk-s">"&lt;your EVE-Cyno API key, optional&gt;"</span>{{end}}
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="linkcards">
      <a class="linkcard" href="{{.CursorInstall}}"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ext"/></svg><span class="lc-t">Add to Cursor</span><svg class="go" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ext"/></svg><span class="lc-s">Opens Cursor and installs eve-cyno{{if .Auth}}, no key{{end}}.</span></a>
      <a class="linkcard" href="{{.VSCodeInstall}}"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ext"/></svg><span class="lc-t">Install in VS Code</span><svg class="go" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ext"/></svg><span class="lc-s">Opens VS Code and installs eve-cyno{{if .Auth}}, no key{{end}}.</span></a>
    </div>
{{if .Auth}}    <p>With an API key: Codex CLI takes <code>--bearer-token-env-var EVE_CYNO_API_KEY</code> (the endpoint accepts <code>Authorization: Bearer</code>; this is the only form that carries a key there), and Gemini CLI takes <code>-H "X-API-Key: ecd_…"</code>. Gemini connects it once the folder is trusted.</p>
{{end}}    <aside class="callout" data-kind="note"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-info"/></svg><div><p class="callout-title">claude.ai and Claude Desktop</p><p>Connector calls reach the server from Anthropic's addresses.{{if .Auth}} Without a key they share one limit per client with every other connector user. {{if .SelfServe}}A free key{{else}}A key{{end}} gives you your own: see <a href="/docs/access#access-keys">API keys</a>.{{end}}</p></div></aside>
    <p>The JSON is the shape the Claude Code plugin ships. Other clients name these fields their own way (Windsurf uses <code>serverUrl</code>; Zed takes <code>url</code> and may add <code>headers</code>): look for an HTTP or streamable-HTTP server setting and give it the URL.</p>
    <p>In Claude Code, check it with <code>claude mcp list</code> (it shows <code>eve-cyno</code> as Connected; in a session, <code>/mcp</code>). <code>--scope user</code> makes the server available in every project; without it, it is saved for the current directory only. Remove it with <code>claude mcp remove eve-cyno --scope user</code>. In Claude Code the tools are named <code>mcp__eve-cyno__&lt;tool&gt;</code>; allow them all with <code>mcp__eve-cyno__*</code>.</p>
    <aside class="callout" data-kind="note"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-info"/></svg><div><p class="callout-title">More harnesses</p><p>Claude Code has a plugin that ships the server, a skill and commands. Every client above connects with the URL alone. If yours is missing, ask on the <a href="https://discord.gg/XZzkH38dt9">EVE-Cyno Discord</a>.</p></div></aside>

    <h2 id="mcp-skill">Agent skill<a class="h-anchor" href="#mcp-skill" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
    <p>The <code>eve-data</code> skill tells an agent which tool to call when, and which attribution to keep. It works with the MCP server and, without MCP, over REST with <code>curl</code>.</p>
    <div class="code" data-copy-scope>
      <div class="code-head"><span class="code-label">Install the skill</span><button class="code-copy" type="button" data-copy aria-label="Copy"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><span data-copy-label>Copy</span></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy>$ </span>mkdir -p ~/.agents/skills/eve-data &amp;&amp; curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eve-cyno/claude-plugins/main/plugins/eve-cyno/skills/eve-data/SKILL.md -o ~/.agents/skills/eve-data/SKILL.md</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor and VS Code read <code>~/.agents/skills</code>. Claude Code reads <code>~/.claude/skills/eve-data/</code> instead: put the file there, or install the plugin, which ships the skill.</p>

    <h2 id="mcp-tools">What the server lists<a class="h-anchor" href="#mcp-tools" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
    <p><code>tools/list</code> follows the access tiers and is chosen per request:</p>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Tier</th><th scope="col">In <code>tools/list</code></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="badge" data-tier="public">public</span></td><td>Always.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="badge" data-tier="keyed">keyed</span></td><td>Only when the caller presents a valid API key.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="badge badge-plain">disabled</span></td><td>Never. Calling one is the protocol's own "unknown tool" error.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2 id="mcp-result">Reading a result<a class="h-anchor" href="#mcp-result" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
    <dl class="fields">
      <dt><code>content[0]</code></dt><dd>The text answer, exactly as REST returns it in <code>result.text</code>.</dd>
      <dt><code>content[1]</code></dt><dd>A short "Sources:" line, when the tool has upstreams. Most clients do not show <code>_meta</code> to the model, and attribution is a condition of several licences.</dd>
      <dt><code>structuredContent</code></dt><dd>The typed result (REST: <code>result.data</code>).</dd>
      <dt><code>_meta</code></dt><dd>The attribution.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2 id="mcp-local">Run it locally (stdio)<a class="h-anchor" href="#mcp-local" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
    <p>The <code>cmd/mcp</code> binary of this module speaks MCP over stdio, for Claude Desktop, Claude Code and other stdio hosts. It reads the SDE from <code>EVE_CORE_SDE_PATH</code>.</p>
    <div class="code" data-copy-scope>
      <div class="code-head"><span class="code-label">core module</span><button class="code-copy" type="button" data-copy aria-label="Copy"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><span data-copy-label>Copy</span></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="tk-p" data-nocopy>$ </span>go run ./cmd/mcp</code></pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="mcp-limits">Limits<a class="h-anchor" href="#mcp-limits" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
    <p>{{.Lim.MCP}} requests per minute{{if .AnonCap}} and {{.AnonCap}} a day{{end}} per {{if .AnonCap}}client without a key{{else}}caller{{end}}{{if .KeysRaise}}, or {{.KeyMCP}} per minute{{if .KeyCap}} and {{.KeyCap}} a day{{end}} with an API key{{else if .KeyCap}}; a key adds a daily cap of {{.KeyCap}} requests{{end}}. A session is a handful of requests (the handshake is three) plus one per tool call. The live tools have one limit of their own, {{.Lim.UpstreamTool}} calls per minute per caller{{if ne .KeyLim.UpstreamTool .Lim.UpstreamTool}} without a key and {{.KeyLim.UpstreamTool}} with one{{end}}, shared with REST. Request bodies are capped at 64 KiB.</p>

    <nav class="pager" aria-label="Previous and next page">
      <a href="/docs/claude-code"><span class="pg-k"><svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-back"/></svg>Previous</span><span class="pg-t">Claude Code plugin</span></a>
